[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Heracles Software Requirements Specification for External GUI
UID: DHF-HRC-0007
METADATA:
  COMPONENT: heracles-external-gui

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @grammar

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Purpose

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The purpose of this document is to provide Software Requirements Specifications for the Heracles External GUI Software.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Scope

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document describes all requirements of the Heracles External GUI Software.

The information in this document is derived from the VoxelRay Heracles Product Requirements Specification, referenced in this document.

*The term Software applies to both Software and Firmware systems.*
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Abbreviations and Definitions

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
GUI
  Graphic User Interface

PRS
  Product Requirements Specification

SDP
  Software Development Plan

SRS
  Software Requirements Specification

SW
  Software
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Overview

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
The external GUI console provides a means for the user to activate and monitor the treatment. It communicates with the main control board and treatment head camera.

The external GUI software runs on the external tablet console located outside the room.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: References

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
Document ID / Reference Number: DHF-HRC-0001
Document Title: Heracles Software Development Plan (SDP)

Document ID / Reference Number: DHF-HRC-0002
Document Title: VoxelRay Product Requirements Specification (PRS)
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
PREFIX: RQ-H10TG-
TITLE: Requirements

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-1
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Daily Warmup
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide a control that allows an operator to initiate a daily warm-up, which will prepare the system for radiation emission.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-1.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-4
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Treatment Parameters Emission Progress indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide a UI indicator that allows users to monitor the progress of emission treatment parameters.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-4.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-8
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Plan details view
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface allowing the operator to view the treatment plan details with the following parameters:

* Treatment fields table - A table view representing the fields as defined in the treatment plan, and includes the following columns:

  * Energy level [kVp].
  * Duration [sec].
  * Current [mA].
  * Actual duration [sec] - A column representing the actual time the emission was delivered.
  * Remaining duration [sec]
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-9
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Beam On process
STATEMENT: >>>
The treatment console shall provide a control that allows the user to initiate/trigger radiation emission.

The interface should include a multi-state control that includes the following states:

* Launch - Triggers the launching phase before beaming on.
* Beam-On - Initiate the radiation emission as the treatment plan requires.
* Reset - Resets the emission parameters, i.e., the timers.

The label of the control should be changed according to its state.

The states will vary from Prepare->Warmup->Load and Launch->Beam On->Reset.

The state of the labels will be changed according to the state machine.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-10
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Emission Progress Indicators
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface allowing the operator to monitor the progress of the delivered emission of a treatment plan.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-10.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-12
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Warmup Progress Monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface that allows the user to monitor the progress of the warm-up prior to the high-voltage ramp-up as part of the Prepare process for a treatment.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-21
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Record Delivered Dose
STATEMENT: >>>
The application should record (save to the database) the time and dose of any radiation delivered in the 'treatment history' for the treated patient.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-22
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Record partial treatment
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall record any partial treatments in a resolution of 0.01 minutes (600 msec) and mark this treatment field as partial in the DB.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-26
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Initialize the System
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall implement functionality to initialize the firmware, instructing it to transition out of the startup state and into the cold state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-29
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Filament Conditioning
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall implement functionality to request filament conditioning from the firmware by specifying the target filament current. The application shall ensure that the target current is within valid operational limits before sending the request to the firmware.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-30
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Perform System Warmup in COLD State
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall implement functionality to request the firmware to perform a warmup procedure, which can only be initiated when the system is in the "COLD" state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-31
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Treatment Plan Staging
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall implement functionality to initiate a new treatment staging by sending a request to the firmware while the system is in the "PRIMED" state. This request shall include the operational point for the treatment plan. The response to the request shall consist of a session ID.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-32
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Load a Treatment Plan
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall implement functionality to load a treatment plan into the firmware.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-34
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Treatment Plan Confirmation
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall receive confirmation responses from the firmware for each operational point in the treatment plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-35
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Confirmation of Treatment Plan
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall confirm the operational point parameters of the treatment plan only after the staging process has been successfully completed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-43
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Radiation Emission Control - Prepare process
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface allowing the user to prepare the system for radiation emission. The preparation will include system warm-up and high voltage ramp-up.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-52
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Enable window switching after emission delivery.
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall enable the left tab bar when the emission is completed, and the plan is unloaded.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-53
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Daily Warmup - Progress Monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface that allows the user to monitor the progress of the warm-up process.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-53.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-57
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Daily Warmup - Log Performed Warmup
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall log all (Full and Fast) warmups performed during the system's lifetime.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-73
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Resume Beam On Process After Error Is Cleared
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall have an interface allowing the user to resume an emission after a fault or interlock is cleared.

When the resume process is triggered, the emission should continue for the remaining duration.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-75
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Resume Prepare process after the error is cleared
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall have a control allowing the user to resume emission preparation after preparation interruption during warmup or high-voltage ramp-up.

The operator will retrigger the Prepare process after clearing the fault or interlock.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-89
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Audit user's actions
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall audit in the system log when the user triggers an action such as:

1. Triggering treatment preparation.
2. Triggering emission delivery.
3. Triggering stop emission
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-90
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Enable Loading a Treatment Plan
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall enable treatment plan loading only during staging periods.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-95
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Emission Progress Indicators
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface allowing the operator to monitor the progress of an emission delivery.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-105
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Reset Timers and Unload Plan after Treatment is Completed
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall clear timers and unload a plan from the board and the UI when the treatment is finished.

The application will prompt the user with a pop-up message when the treatment is finished, and the emission is delivered successfully.

The info message will include an OK control, triggering a timer reset and unloading the plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-160
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Load For Treatment - Resume Uncompleted Treatment Alert
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall alert the operator if the loaded plan was not completely delivered and enable the operator to choose to deliver the remaining plan (i.e., resume the treatment) or deliver the whole treatment plan.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-161
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Load For Treatment - Resume Uncompleted Treatment
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall enable the operator to resume uncompleted treatment. In case the last treatment was stopped in the middle and the delivery of the treatment plan was not completed, the operator should be able to resume the delivery of the remaining treatment.

When a plan is loaded, the application should query the latest treatment and check if this treatment is marked as completed. If not, it will pop up a message to the user about the uncompleted treatment.

If the user chooses to resume the treatment, the application should calculate the remaining time and use this as the plan to be delivered.

If the user chooses not to resume, the plan should be loaded as is, and the whole treatment should be delivered.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-247
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Prevent user from starting an emission due to delta between magnetometers
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall prevent the user from starting an emission if the delta between the Front Magnetometer and Back Magnetometer correction values is larger than maxMagnetomerDiff. The Front Magnetometer and Back Magnetometer Correction Matrix values will be fetched from the DB.

The MaxMagnetomerDiff should be defined in the machine's HeadConfiguration.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-279
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Allow Quality Checks with Dedicated Collimator only
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall automatically identify that the dedicated QC collimator is connected. It should allow the operator to perform Quality Checks only if this is the connected collimator.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-280
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Physics View
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface that enables an authorized user to initiate an emission procedure to measure the quality of the beam.

The user shall be able to select the Applicator type that is used and to set the beam parameters: Energy, Duration.

Once an applicator and Energy are set, the Coils (X, Y, and Focus) and Heater Current that are configured for this Applicator will be populated to the UI.

The application should alert the user if the connected applicator is different from the selected one.

The emission process shall include the emission actions: Prepare, Beam-On, and Stop. All safety interlocks shall be cleared before emission.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-280.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-281
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: On-Screen Keyboard Adjustable Position
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide the user with the ability to reposition the On-Screen Keyboard on the screen so that it does not block critical interface components.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-2
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Telemetry
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface that displays immutable semantic telemetry
received from the control-board firmware in real time, including:

* Control-board state and firmware mode
* Emission and backup timers
* Emission current and energy
* Safety interlocks and system-fault categories

The application shall select the telemetry layout from the reported firmware version and
mode. A field that is not supplied by that firmware mode shall be shown as unavailable
rather than as a false or zero measurement.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-3
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Stop Emission
STATEMENT: >>>
The treatment console shall include a stop control that allows the user to immediately terminate radiation emissions.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-3.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-5
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Emission visible indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
The treatment console shall provide a visible indicator for the entire time the X-rays are produced.

The visual indication of X-ray emission will be provided by a glowing radiation icon Amber color.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-36
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Treatment Plan Execution Condition
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall prevent treatment plan execution if an interlock is active. The 'Beam-On' button will be disabled.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-49
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Restrict window switching during active emission
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall temporarily lock the treatment view interface during active radiation delivery.

The left tab bar shall be disabled.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-66
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Perform Quality Checks
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide the operator with an interface to test and record the quality of the beam.

Before triggering the emission, the operator will set the Energy for which to perform the quality tests.

The measured intensity will be recorded for each point.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-66.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-82
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Telemetry - No communication to GCB indication
STATEMENT: >>>
The telemetry controls shall show a clear no-communication indication when no valid
telemetry has been received from the GCB for 1.5 seconds. Stale telemetry values shall no
longer be presented as current; affected values shall be shown as unavailable.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-82.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-85
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Patient Details
STATEMENT: >>>
The treatment console shall display details about the treated patient and its treatment site.

The patient details shall include the following:

* Patient full name
* MRN
* Patient DOB
* Field Name
* Dose to be delivered (per fraction)
* Collimator Type (Target Type)
* Field/Shield Size
* Devices
* Setup Notes (Simulation notes)

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-85.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-86
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Patient Monitoring
STATEMENT: >>>
The treatment console shall display a live view of the treated patient for monitoring.

The live monitoring will enable the user to stop the emission in case of a patient crisis or movement.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-86.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-87
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Emission audible indicator
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an audible indicator for the entire time the X-rays are produced.

The indicator should be a plus of half a second on/off with 1 -2 KHz or similar.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-91
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Perform System Safety Checks
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide the operator with an interface to test and record system safety features:

The operator will have the controls to prepare and activate the system for radiation. During the radiation, the user will check the:

1. X-ray light - A visual indicator that the X-ray is activated.
2. X-ray sound - An audible indication that the X-ray is activated
3. Door interlock - Open the door and check that the radiation stops.
4. E-stop - Press the physical stop button and check that the radiation stops.
5. Normal stop - Press the applicative stop and ensure the radiation is stopped.
6. Live video stream - Check that the live camera on the radiation head is working and the room is monitored.
7. Live audio stream - Check that the live audio on the device is working.

For each test, the user will toggle the corresponding success/failure button.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-91.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-92
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Quality Assurance - System Safety Checks Reports
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide the operator with an interface to display the history of test results which includes the following system safety features: X-Ray light, X-Ray sound, door interlock, estop, normal stop, live video stream, and live audio stream between the patient and operator.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-91-1.png
.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-91-2.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-93
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Quality Checks Reports
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide the operator with an interface displaying the history of quality test results.

The results will include the current and the intensity for each operational point.

The operator will be able to filter the results by the applicator type, energy level, and the date the test was performed.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-93.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-94
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Quality Checks Reports - Deviation
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide the operator with an interface displaying the history of quality test results.

The results will include the current and the deviation from the referenced test for each test point (Diode) .
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-96
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Prevent Treatment if the Daily Safety checks is not completed
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall prevent treatment if there is no record of safety checks performed on the day of the treatment or if safety checks are not completed.

A safety check is not completed if the following features were not tested or failed: door interlock, e-stop, and normal stop.

The application will display an error pop-up message to the operator stating that the treatment cannot be delivered if the safety checks are not completed.

The pop-up message will be shown when the user presses the Prepare control.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-97
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Alert for uncompleted Daily Safety checks
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall display a warning pop-up message if the daily safety checks are uncompleted.

The warning message will be displayed if and only if the following features are successfully tested: door interlock, e-stop, and normal stop, and the following features were not tested or failed:

X-Ray light, X-Ray sound, live video stream, and live audio stream.

The application will display a warning pop-up message to the operator asking the user to confirm the treatment even though the safety checks are uncompleted.

The pop-up message will be shown when the user presses the Prepare control.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-106
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Quality Assurance - Perform System Safety Checks - Save Results
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide a control enabling the user to save the safety test results in the database.

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-106.png
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-139
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment View - Safety Interlocks
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall provide an interface that displays the semantic state of all safety
interlocks. An available interlock shall indicate ready or active; an interlock not supplied
by the selected firmware mode shall indicate unavailable.

The application will have a dedicated control that, when clicked by the user, will display
a pop-up with the list of interlocks.

The interlocks should include:

* Applicator
* Remote Key
* Door -
* Base E-Stop
* Remote E-Stop
* Timer #1
* Timer #2
* Water Level
* Head
* HVPS
* Cooler Alarm
* Watchdog
* Ion pump
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-282
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment - Prevent Treatment Initiation for Unapproved Failed QC Tests
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall prevent treatment initiation within the Treatment View if any Quality Control (QC) test associated with the energy level and applicator type required by the treatment plan has failed and has not been manually approved by an authorized user.

When the user attempts to initiate treatment (press the Prepare button), the application will:

* Verify the energy level(s) used in the current treatment plan.
* The system shall check the latest QC status for the plan's applicator and energy level. (i.e., the deviation from the reference values exceeds a predefined threshold).
* If the corresponding QC test has failed, verify that a user has approved it. If it is not approved, an alert message will be displayed to the user, and the treatment operation will be blocked.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-283
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Treatment - Prevent a Treatment When There Is No Approved Physics Data
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall prevent the user from starting clinical emission exposure (treatment) when no approved physics data is available in the system.

When the user presses the prepare button, an error message will pop up with a message such as: 'Treatment cannot be started. Approved physics data is required.'
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-284
TYPE: Functional
TITLE: Treatment View - Active Fault Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The application shall display the currently latched control-board fault records. Each
record shall show the fault category, formatted message, and the system state and runtime
captured when the fault occurred.

The application shall retrieve multi-entry fault snapshots by index, keep the displayed
list synchronized with unsolicited fault and clear notifications, and provide a command to
clear the latched records. Up to four simultaneously active records shall be displayed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-285
TYPE: Safety
TITLE: Disable Clinical Functions in Calibration Mode
STATEMENT: >>>
When the connected control board reports calibration firmware mode, the application shall
disable the Treatment and Quality Assurance tabs and obscure their content with a message
directing the user to service the device. Non-clinical service, log, and exit functions
shall remain accessible.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: RQ-H10TG-13
TYPE: Usability
TITLE: Treatment View - Layout
STATEMENT: >>>
The user shall have an interface through which they can initiate radiation delivery according to a predefined treatment plan.

The interface shall be accessible via a console located outside of the treatment room to ensure safety and compliance with radiation safety regulations.

The layout should include:

1. Patient Identification
2. The plan's treatment fields.
3. The system telemetry: System status, Main timer (in sec), backup timers (T1 & T2) (in sec), Energy (in kV), and Current (in mA).
4. Activation buttons:

   1. Prepare button - which will prepare the system for radiation (i.e., warm-up and loading).
   2. Beam-On/Reset/Clear error - a multi-state control for triggering the emission, resetting timers, and clearing errors.
   3. Stop button - Stops the emission.

5. Interlocks visualization.
6. System Signals
7. Live Camera to monitor the patient.
8. System readiness indicators

.. image:: _images/RQ-H10TG-13.png
<<<

[[/SECTION]]
